input: Keep the first character typed into the search panel

Since 0660be4c, set_search_query anchors a changed query to the viewport.
The panel's own typing calls it, so the first character moves the anchor
from None to the viewport start. The overlay compared anchors to tell the
panel's echo from an outside change, so it re-showed the panel, which
selects the query, and the next keystroke replaced it: typing "Docker"
after opening search left "ocker".

An anchor change is now part of the echo when the panel already holds the
session's query. Opening search again still re-shows the panel, because it
bumps the activation revision.

Send upstream; remove once GPUI Kit releases the fix.

diff --git a/src/input/overlay.rs b/src/input/overlay.rs
index 3de83ae..f506939 100644
--- a/src/input/overlay.rs
+++ b/src/input/overlay.rs
@@ -354,12 +354,14 @@ impl<M: OverlayMode> InputOverlayHost<M> {
             // session. Re-showing it for that echo would select the query or steal
             // focus from replacement, so preserve changes the panel already holds.
             // External mode changes still move focus out of a hidden replace field.
+            // A query typed in the panel also anchors the session to the viewport.
+            // That anchor is part of the echo: re-showing would select the first
+            // typed character, and the next keystroke would replace it.
             let was = &self.search_signature;
             let query_echo = search_open
                 && was.open
                 && (was.replace_mode == search_signature.replace_mode
                     || panel_replace_mode == search_signature.replace_mode)
-                && was.anchor_offset == search_signature.anchor_offset
                 && was.activation_revision == search_signature.activation_revision
                 && self.search.read(cx).query(cx) == search_session.query;
             self.search_signature = search_signature;
